CI was failing due to deprecated syntax in documentation examples. The MoonBit compiler now treats deprecated syntax as errors with `--deny-warn`.

## Changes

**Test parameter type (24 instances)**
```moonbit
// Before
test "example" (t : @test.T) { ... }

// After  
test "example" (t : @test.Test) { ... }
```

**Trait alias syntax**
```moonbit
// Before
traitalias @builtin.Compare as CanCompare

// After
using @builtin { trait Compare as CanCompare }
```

**Type alias in sudoku example**
```moonbit
// Before
typealias @immut/sorted_set.SortedSet[String] as Squares

// After
type Squares = @immut/sorted_set.SortedSet[String]
```

**Array literal annotation**
