This PR introduces a conversion API for extracting typed data from `gr::pmt::Value` into STL containers and Tensor types. The design provides compile-time policy control over type conversion, shape handling, and PMR memory handling, with `std::expected`-based error handling.

---

## TL;DR – Typical Usage
```cpp
using namespace gr::pmt;

Value v{Tensor<float>{data_from, {1.5f, 2.5f, 3.5f}}};
```

### 1. Basic Extraction with `convertTo<T>()`
```cpp
// same-type extraction
auto vec = convertTo<std::vector<float>>(v);           // std::expected<vector<float>, ConversionError>
if (vec) {
    std::println("size = {}", vec->size());
}

// with type widening
auto dvec = convertTo<std::vector<double>, ConversionPolicy::Widening>(v);

// with fallback on failure
auto safe = convertTo_or<std::vector<float>>(v, std::vector<float>{});
auto lazy = convertTo_or<std::vector<float>>(v, [] { return std::vector<float>{}; });
```

### 2. In-Place Assignment with `assignTo()`
```cpp
std::vector<float> dst;
dst.reserve(1000);                                     // pre-allocate

assignTo(dst, v);                                      // reuses capacity, no reallocation
assignTo<ConversionPolicy::Widening>(dst, value);      // with type conversion
assignTo(dst, std::move(v));                           // move optimization
```

### 3. Map Extraction (Value-typed and Typed)
```cpp
Value mapVal{std::map<std::string, int>{{"a", 1}, {"b", 2}}};

// To Value-typed map
auto valMap = convertTo<std::map<std::string, Value>>(mapVal);

// To typed map (same type)
auto intMap = convertTo<std::map<std::string, int>>(mapVal);

// To typed map (with widening)
auto dblMap = convertTo<std::map<std::string, double>, ConversionPolicy::Widening>(mapVal);
```

### 4. Heterogeneous `Tensor<Value>` Extraction
```cpp
Value hetero{Tensor<Value>{Value{1}, Value{2}, Value{3}}};

// Extract if all elements are convertible to the target type
auto ints = convertTo<std::vector<int>>(hetero);

// With type conversion policy
auto floats = convertTo<std::vector<float>, ConversionPolicy::Widening>(hetero);
```

---

## For Reviewers – Motivation

Extracting typed data from `gr::pmt::Value` previously required manual type-checking and casting at each call site. This led to:

1. **Boilerplate**: Repeated `holds<T>()` / `get_if<T>()` patterns scattered throughout the codebase.

2. **Inconsistent Error Handling**: Some sites threw, some returned nullopt, some asserted.

3. **No Type Conversion Control**: Implicit conversions could silently lose precision or fail unexpectedly.

4. **Allocation Waste**: Each extraction allocated fresh storage even when existing capacity was available.

`ValueHelper` addresses these issues with a unified, policy-driven API that makes conversion semantics explicit at the call site.

---

## Design

### Three Orthogonal Policies

**ConversionPolicy** – Controls numeric type coercion:

| Policy | Allows | Use Case |
|--------|--------|----------|
| `Safe` | Exact type match only | Strict type discipline |
| `Widening` | + lossless promotions (int32→int64, float→double) | Safe numeric interop |
| `Narrowing` | + potentially lossy (double→float, int64→int32) | Known-safe truncation |
| `Unchecked` | Any `static_cast`-able conversion | Performance-critical paths |

**RankPolicy** – Controls tensor shape handling:

| Policy | Behavior | Use Case |
|--------|----------|----------|
| `Strict` | Rank and extents must match exactly | Shape-sensitive algorithms |
| `Flatten` | Any rank → rank-1 (linearizes) | Bulk data processing |
| `Reshape` | Size-preserving reshape | Dimension reinterpretation |

**ResourcePolicy** – Controls PMR memory allocation:

| Policy | Behavior | Use Case |
|--------|----------|----------|
| `UseDefault` | Use provided or default PMR resource | Normal operation |
| `InheritFromSource` | Use source Value's PMR resource | Arena-local extraction |

### Supported Conversions

| Source | Target | Notes |
|--------|--------|-------|
| `Tensor<T>` | `std::vector<U>` | Type conversion per policy |
| `Tensor<T>` | `std::array<U, N>` | Size must match |
| `Tensor<T>` | `Tensor<U, ...>` | Shape validation per RankPolicy |
| `Tensor<Value>` | Any of above | Element-wise extraction |
| `Map<string, Value>` | `std::map<string, Value>` | Direct copy |
| `Map<string, Value>` | `std::unordered_map<string, Value>` | Direct copy |
| `Map<string, Value>` | `std::map<string, T>` | Element-wise type conversion |
| `Map<string, Value>` | `std::unordered_map<string, T>` | Element-wise type conversion |

---

## Error Handling

All operations return `std::expected<T, ConversionError>` with structured error information:
```cpp
struct ConversionError {
    enum class Kind { 
        TypeMismatch, ElementTypeMismatch, RankMismatch, 
        ExtentsMismatch, SizeMismatch, NotATensor, NotAMap,
        NarrowingNotAllowed, WideningNotAllowed 
    };
    Kind kind;
    std::string_view message;
    std::size_t index;  // For element-wise errors (dynamic_extent if N/A)
    
    [[nodiscard]] bool hasIndex() const noexcept;
};
```

Example error handling:
```cpp
auto result = convertTo<std::vector<int>>(mixedTensorValue);
if (!result) {
    if (result.error().kind == ConversionError::Kind::ElementTypeMismatch) {
        std::println("Type mismatch at index {}", result.error().index);
    }
}
```

---

## Relationship to Value's Monadic API

`ValueHelper` complements `Value`'s monadic accessors:

| Use Case | Preferred API |
|----------|---------------|
| Single scalar extraction | `value.value_or<T>()`, `value.get_if<T>()` |
| Tensor → STL container | `convertTo<std::vector<T>>(value)` |
| Tensor → Tensor (different type) | `convertTo<Tensor<U>>(value)` |
| Map → typed map | `convertTo<std::map<string, T>>(value)` |
| In-place with capacity reuse | `assignTo(dst, value)` |

The monadic API handles scalar and simple access patterns; `ValueHelper` handles bulk container conversions with policy control.
